1
00:00:06,710 --> 00:00:09,890
A shop takes 35 percent off everything.

2
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:12,680
A jacket costs 120 dollars.

3
00:00:12,730 --> 00:00:16,450
Can you find the sale price in one calculation?

4
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:19,710
What is 120 dollars with 35 percent off?

5
00:00:19,760 --> 00:00:23,730
Pause the video and work it out.

6
00:00:23,780 --> 00:00:30,210
If 35 percent is taken off, you pay 100 minus 35, which is 65 percent.

7
00:00:30,260 --> 00:00:33,720
65 percent as a decimal is 0.65.

8
00:00:33,770 --> 00:00:35,690
So multiply by 0.65.

9
00:00:35,740 --> 00:00:38,550
120 times 0.65 is 78 dollars.

10
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:41,470
That is one calculation.

11
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:46,980
Remember: 35 percent is 0.35, and 100 percent is 1.

12
00:00:47,030 --> 00:00:49,690
108 percent is 1.08.

13
00:00:49,740 --> 00:00:53,260
A multiplier changes an amount in one step.

14
00:00:53,310 --> 00:00:59,080
After a 15 percent increase you have 115 percent, so multiply by 1.15.

15
00:00:59,130 --> 00:01:05,360
After a 35 percent decrease you have 65 percent, so multiply by 0.65.

16
00:01:05,410 --> 00:01:06,090
Your turn.

17
00:01:06,140 --> 00:01:09,690
What is the multiplier for a 22 percent decrease?

18
00:01:09,740 --> 00:01:13,070
Pause the video and try it.

19
00:01:13,120 --> 00:01:15,870
100 minus 22 is 78 percent.

20
00:01:15,920 --> 00:01:19,120
So the multiplier is 0.78.

21
00:01:19,170 --> 00:01:22,730
Multipliers also work for repeated changes.

22
00:01:22,780 --> 00:01:28,270
Two 10 percent rises is times 1.1, times 1.1, which is times 1.21.

23
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:32,350
That is a 21 percent rise, not 20 percent.

24
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:33,850
Here is the method.

25
00:01:33,900 --> 00:01:39,710
Step 1: for an increase of r percent, the multiplier is 1 plus r over 100.

26
00:01:39,760 --> 00:01:43,510
For a decrease, it is 1 minus r over 100.

27
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:48,050
Step 2: multiply the original amount by the multiplier.

28
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:53,210
Step 3: for several changes, multiply the multipliers together.

29
00:01:53,260 --> 00:01:54,280
Step 4: check.

30
00:01:54,330 --> 00:01:57,090
An increase has a multiplier above 1.

31
00:01:57,140 --> 00:01:59,690
A decrease has one below 1.

32
00:01:59,740 --> 00:02:05,720
A car worth 14,000 dollars loses 18 percent of its value.

33
00:02:05,770 --> 00:02:08,150
The multiplier is 0.82.

34
00:02:08,200 --> 00:02:12,500
14,000 times 0.82 is 11,480 dollars.

35
00:02:12,550 --> 00:02:13,390
Your turn.

36
00:02:13,440 --> 00:02:17,400
Increase 500 by 12 percent, using times 1.12.

37
00:02:17,450 --> 00:02:20,760
Pause and work it out.

38
00:02:20,810 --> 00:02:24,400
500 times 1.12 is 560.

39
00:02:24,450 --> 00:02:28,490
A price rises 20 percent, then falls 20 percent.

40
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:30,870
Is it back where it started?

41
00:02:30,920 --> 00:02:34,490
Times 1.2, times 0.8, is times 0.96.

42
00:02:34,540 --> 00:02:36,030
0.96 is 96 percent.

43
00:02:36,080 --> 00:02:39,110
So overall it is a 4 percent decrease.

44
00:02:39,160 --> 00:02:41,930
It is not back to the start.

45
00:02:41,980 --> 00:02:44,730
A value is multiplied by 1.035.

46
00:02:44,780 --> 00:02:47,520
What percentage change is that?

47
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:53,120
1.035 is 103.5 percent, so it is a 3.5 percent increase.

48
00:02:53,170 --> 00:02:56,030
Lee decreases 90 dollars by 30 percent.

49
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:58,670
Which line goes wrong first?

50
00:02:58,720 --> 00:02:59,990
Line 1 is wrong.

51
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:02,890
0.3 finds the 30 percent taken off.

52
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:08,830
After the decrease you keep 70 percent, so the multiplier is 0.7.

53
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:12,410
90 times 0.7 is 63 dollars.

54
00:03:12,460 --> 00:03:15,840
Banks pay interest as a percentage each year.

55
00:03:15,890 --> 00:03:21,500
With 5 percent interest, savings are multiplied by 1.05 every year.

56
00:03:21,550 --> 00:03:30,770
1,000 dollars becomes 1,000 times 1.05 times 1.05, which is 1,102 dollars 50, after 2 years.

57
00:03:30,820 --> 00:03:34,540
The interest earns interest too.

58
00:03:34,590 --> 00:03:35,860
One last question.

59
00:03:35,910 --> 00:03:39,740
Multiplying by 1.1 twice is what percentage increase?

60
00:03:39,790 --> 00:03:43,120
Pause the video and answer.

61
00:03:43,170 --> 00:03:47,190
1.1 times 1.1 is 1.21, which is 121 percent.

62
00:03:47,240 --> 00:03:50,600
So it is a 21 percent increase.

63
00:03:50,650 --> 00:03:56,430
To remember: for an increase of r percent, multiply by 1 plus r over 100.

64
00:03:56,480 --> 00:04:00,730
For a decrease, multiply by 1 minus r over 100.

65
00:04:00,780 --> 00:04:03,890
One calculation gives the new amount.

66
00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:07,800
For repeated changes, multiply the multipliers.

67
00:04:07,850 --> 00:04:12,250
You can turn a multiplier back into a percentage change.

68
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:17,630
Great work! Now practise lesson 10.2 on Camday.
